{%- case gem_handle -%}

  {%- when 'navratana' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--navratana">
    <h2>Why Navratna Exists</h2>
    <b>Because Balance Is Different From Strength</b>
    <p>Most astrological gemstones are traditionally worn to strengthen a particular planetary influence.</p>
    <p>Navratna exists for a different reason.</p>
    <p>Rather than focusing on one force, it brings together all nine planetary gemstones within a single arrangement. The traditional belief is that harmony arises when each planetary influence is acknowledged and none is allowed to dominate the others.</p>
    <p>Its purpose is not to make one voice louder.</p>
    <p>It is to help the whole system remain balanced.</p>
  </div>

  {%- when 'upratnas' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--upratnas">
    <h2>Why Upratnas Exist</h2>
    <b>Because Tradition Allows More Than One Path</b>
    <p>Astrological traditions have always recognised that different people require different remedies.</p>
    <p>For some, a primary planetary gemstone may be recommended. For others, a supporting gemstone may be considered more suitable due to personal circumstances, comfort level, practicality, or astrological guidance.</p>
    <p>Upratna exist because traditional gemstone practice has never been based solely on rarity or price. It has always acknowledged that effectiveness, comfort, and suitability can take many forms.</p>
    <p>These gemstones allow individuals to participate in a centuries-old tradition while respecting their own preferences and circumstances.</p>
    <p>The purpose of an Upratna is not to be stronger.</p>
    <p>It is to be appropriate.</p>
  </div>

  {%- when 'beyond-nine' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--beyond_nine">
    <h2>Why Beyond Nine Exists</h2>
    <b>Because Not Every Gemstone Needs a Reason</b>
    <p>For centuries, gemstones have been worn for symbolism, status, astrology, and tradition.</p>
    <p>But some gemstones transcend categories.</p>
    <p>They are chosen not because a chart suggests them, but because they create an immediate connection. A colour unlike any other. A phenomenon that feels impossible. A beauty that refuses to be explained.</p>
    <p>Beyond Nine was created for those stones.</p>
    <p>The ones collected for wonder.</p>
    <p>The ones purchased for admiration.</p>
    <p>The ones that remind us that sometimes beauty is reason enough.</p>
  </div>

 
{%- when 'sacred-essentials' -%}
<div class="gem-tab gem-tab--sacred_essentials">
  <h2>Why Sacred Essentials Exists</h2>
  <b>For many people, the journey begins with a recommendation.</b>
  <p>An astrologer suggests a gemstone.</p>
  <p>But what follows often feels intimidating.</p>
  <p>High gemstone prices.</p>
  <p>Expensive jewellery settings.</p>
  <p>Pressure-driven selling.</p>
  <p>What begins as belief slowly becomes hesitation.</p>
  <p>Not because people stop believing.</p>
  <p>Because the process stops feeling accessible.</p>
  <p>Sacred Essentials was created to remove that barrier.</p>
  <p>To make authentic gemstone traditions available without unnecessary pressure, confusion, or financial discomfort.</p>
</div>


{%- when 'sanctum' -%}
<div class="gem-tab gem-tab--sanctum">
  <h2>Why Sanctum Exists</h2>
  <b>Because Some Stones Deserve a Different Standard</b>
  <p>Most gemstones are evaluated for beauty.</p>
  <p>The rarest gemstones are evaluated for significance.</p>
  <p>Sanctum exists to bring together stones that stand apart because of their rarity, origin, quality, or historical importance.</p>
  <p>These are gemstones that collectors search for over years, not days.</p>
  <p>Some represent exceptional geological events.</p>
  <p>Some originate from legendary sources.</p>
  <p>Some simply possess a combination of colour, clarity, and character that is unlikely to be encountered again.</p>
  <p>Because certain gemstones deserve more than a listing.</p>
  <p>They deserve context.</p>
</div>


{%- when 'crush-worthy-delights' -%}
<div class="gem-tab gem-tab--crush_worthy_delights">
  <h2>Why Crush Worthy Delights Exists</h2>
  <b>Because Joy Deserves a Place Too</b>
  <p>Many gemstone collections focus on rarity, investment value, or astrological significance.</p>
  <p>Crush Worthy Delights was created for something simpler.</p>
  <p>The pleasure of discovering a gemstone that immediately feels right.</p>
  <p>A colour that catches your eye.</p>
  <p>A sparkle that makes you smile.</p>
  <p>A stone that feels personal without needing a deeper explanation.</p>
  <p>Because gemstones do not always have to be serious.</p>
  <p>Sometimes they are simply beautiful.</p>
  <p>And that is enough.</p>
</div>


{%- when 'strand-edit' -%}
<div class="gem-tab gem-tab--strand_edit">
  <h2>Why Strand Edit Exists</h2>
  <b>Because Some Gemstones Deserve Freedom</b>
  <p>Most gemstones eventually become a finished piece of jewellery.</p>
  <p>A strand remains something more open.</p>
  <p>It can be worn as it is, redesigned into something personal, used in spiritual practice, or simply admired as a collection of natural beauty.</p>
  <p>Strand Edit was created to celebrate that flexibility.</p>
  <p>To offer gemstones not as finished statements, but as creative beginnings.</p>
  <p>Because sometimes the most beautiful thing about a gemstone is what it has yet to become.</p>
</div>


  {%- else -%}
  <div class="gem-tab">
    <p>[Placeholder] Content coming soon.</p>
  </div>

{%- endcase -%}
